    "result_text": "All 29 tests pass with a green build. \n\nThe change is implemented following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step reading the request DTO's city, counting existing owners in that city (case-insensitive, trimmed, mirroring `AssignCustomerCode`'s normalization), and throwing when the count reaches the cap of 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception carrying the city and current count.\n- **`CityAtCapacityHandler`** + **escalation YAML** \u2014 turns the exception into a **409 Conflict** `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"city\"]`, matching the shape of the existing duplicate-household/telephone handlers.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserts the `checkCityCapacity` step (governed by `transaction`) after the household check and before `build`.\n\nThe 51st owner in a full city is rejected with 409, exactly as `Cp18Tests` expects, and no existing checkpoint regressed.",
